Z||000000||yellowTee||06-26-2001||09:40 AM||||I hope you guys can help me!  I have had this problem on my 84 2.5 for the past few mounths.  When I first start the car the alt gauge reads above 13. After I drive for a while the gauge comes down slightly.  the problem comes in if the headlights are on when I come to a stoplight, step on the brake and sit at the light.  The gauge drops to almost 11 then it never comes back up even after I start driving again.  I have been pulling my hair out.  I have replaced the alt. checked the battery connections, unhooked all the wires in the engine and cleaned and polished them.  I don't know what else to try!!! Is this normal and I am just nuts or what.  Please help me!!!<P>------------------<BR>84 white 2m4<BR>88 yellow t-top, factory||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||06-26-2001||03:05 PM||||'Fit were me, first thing I'd try, is to carry a voltmeter with me, and then when the gage reads consistently low as you describe, find a safe place to pull over. Check the battery voltage with the meter <B>at</B> the battery, to see if the dash gage is lying to you.<P>     ||||reg||3
Z||000002||johnt671||06-26-2001||06:16 PM||||I had the same problem last week.  The gauge always read 15 and then started to go up or down below 13 w/o reason.  I checked all of the charging system and found on bad connections and replaced the alternator, which cured the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||yellowTee||06-27-2001||09:28 AM||||Thanks for the suggestion.  I did just replace the alt, and it didn't seem to help.  I will have to carry a voltmeter to see if the gauge is lying or if I got a bad alt. thanks again I will let you know what I find out.<P>------------------<BR>84 white 2m4<BR>88 yellow t-top, factory||||reg||1
